{
  "id": "typescript-17-isolated-modules-verbatim",
  "slug": "isolated-modules-verbatim",
  "title": "isolatedModules, verbatimModuleSyntax, and bundler emit",
  "moduleId": "typescript-17-compiler-options-tooling",
  "order": 2,
  "hook": "**isolatedModules** ensures per-file transpile for Babel/esbuild. **verbatimModuleSyntax** forces `import type` — TS 5+ clean emit.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "isolatedModules forbids cross-file const enum inline etc. verbatimModuleSyntax requires type imports use **import type**. Pair moduleResolution bundler for Vite. const enum problematic with isolatedModules — use as const."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "isolatedModules",
              "longForm": "per-file transpile",
              "plainDefinition": "Each file standalone emit unit.",
              "example": "true for bundlers"
            },
            {
              "term": "verbatimModuleSyntax",
              "longForm": "import type",
              "plainDefinition": "Type imports must use import type.",
              "example": "import type { User }"
            },
            {
              "term": "const enum",
              "longForm": "isolated conflict",
              "plainDefinition": "Inlining needs cross-file — breaks isolated.",
              "example": "use as const"
            },
            {
              "term": "transpileModule",
              "longForm": "single file API",
              "plainDefinition": "Babel/esbuild per-file.",
              "example": "needs isolated rules"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Vite fails on const enum. Mixed imports cause runtime import of type-only module."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: import { Type }",
          "body": "verbatimModuleSyntax: interface import must be import type."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "isolatedModules true",
              "body": "Set isolatedModules so each file transpiles independently — required for Babel/esbuild/swc."
            },
            {
              "title": "verbatimModuleSyntax",
              "body": "TS5+"
            },
            {
              "title": "replace const enum",
              "body": "as const"
            },
            {
              "title": "split imports",
              "body": "type vs value"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "per-file transpile",
            "source": "flowchart LR\n  F1 --> ES[esbuild]\n  F2 --> ES\n  ISO[isolatedModules] --> ES"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "json",
            "label": "Vite tsconfig",
            "code": "{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"verbatimModuleSyntax\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}",
            "explanation": "Standard frontend config."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "import type",
            "code": "import type { User } from \"./types\";\nimport { createUser } from \"./types\";",
            "explanation": "Split type/value."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "as const not const enum",
            "code": "const Direction = { Up: \"up\", Down: \"down\" } as const;\ntype Direction = typeof Direction[keyof typeof Direction];",
            "explanation": "Bundler-safe enum alternative."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: type import runtime",
            "code": "import { Config } from \"./config\"; // type-only interface — bad emit without verbatim",
            "explanation": "Runtime import empty module."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
